# FINAL FANTASY IX (Japan), the codes of its messages.
# One byte a character; kanji are two bytes, 0xFA-0xFE and a second. Control codes (0xF7 a line break, 0xF8,
# 0xF9 with its arguments, 0xFF the end) are the script's business and aren't here.
# Kana, by rule: hiragana from 0x56 in gojuon order with the small vowels after the vowels and each row's
# voiced rows after it; katakana 0x50 higher. Found by entering a name a character at a time and reading the
# name's bytes, and checked on the lines of the first scene.
# Digits and letters are read off the game's own debug messages, not off the screen.
# Kanji 0xFA nn and 0xFB nn, the same in every place: read off the game's own glyph pictures, drawn from its
# glyph list and video memory, and checked by reading messages decoded with them. Nineteen glyphs whose reading
# stayed in doubt are left out. Codes from 0xFC 00 differ by place: the script's file of places.
